Id: con018e
Severity: ERROR
Category: tigris
Check: config
Fix: chown the directory to root (or your own user, running with sudo) and chmod 700 it; or name another with -w or -l.
References: tigris(8)

The working directory (-w) or the log directory (-l) belongs to someone
other than root, the user running Tigris or the user who invoked sudo,
or its group or others may write it. Tigris creates its files there
under names a bystander could guess and follows a symbolic link it finds
in their place, as root, so a directory someone else can write into is
not used.
